-- title:
--   Valuation subrings over a DVR pinned by separable approximants
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $M$ be fields with $M$ a $K$-algebra, and let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring in the local-ring sense) together with an $O$-algebra structure on $M$ whose structure map $O \to M$ is injective, and such that the image of every $c \in K$ in $M$ lies in the image of $O \to M$. Let $E$ be a subfield of $M$ each of whose elements $x$ is separable over $K$, i.e. has separable minimal polynomial over $K$, and assume that the subfield of $M$ generated by the union of the image of $O \to M$ and $E$ is all of $M$. Let $V$ and $V'$ be valuation subrings of $M$, each containing the image of $O \to M$, such that for every $b$ in the maximal ideal of $O$ both $V$-valuation and $V'$-valuation of the image of $b$ are $< 1$, and such that every $b \in O$ admits a single element $c \in E$ with the $V$-valuation and the $V'$-valuation of (image of $b$) $- \, c$ both $< 1$. Then $V = V'$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the standard statement that, in an extension of $M$ generated over a discrete valuation ring $O$ by constants separable over a base field $K$ mapping into $O$, a valuation subring lying over $O$ and centred on the maximal ideal of $O$ is determined by the residues it assigns to elements of $O$: the common approximants in $E$ select one and the same prime above the maximal ideal. It is used in the comparison of prolongations of places on modular curves, through [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_reduceFst_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_reduceFst_eq).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_eq_of_forall_exists_sub_valuation_lt_one.lean

